[2.488195, "o", "│  SSE stream open. heartbeats keep every timeout alive. client: spinner,\r\n│  no read timeout set. server: batch slot held. billing: per token.\r\n"]
[2.488319, "o", "│  \u001b[2mnothing is broken anywhere. that's the terrifying part.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m┌─ L6 · THE ORCHESTRATOR — the loop lives where meaning lives \u001b[2m────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m│  vLLM-style server · CUDA graphs · continuous batching\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.593386, "o", "│  the loop isn't a for-statement a human wrote — it's a scheduler calling\r\n│  generate() forever because nothing defines 'done'. \u001b[31mthe only layer\r\n"]
[2.593514, "o", "│  where 'meaning' still exists — the only layer where the loop can be broken.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m│  watchdog inventory: client 0 · gateway 0 · scheduler 0 · sampler 0\u001b[0m\r\n│  in field sessions, the only layer that ever stops the loop is the human:\r\n│  \u001b[33mCtrl+C, 4/4. the human layer outperformed every automated layer.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m┌─ L7 · CUDA KERNEL — the spiral, written in C \u001b[2m───────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
